# Task Manager API

A simple REST API built with Node.js and Express for managing tasks.

## Features

- GET /health - Check if the API is running
- GET /tasks - Get all tasks
- GET /tasks/:id - Get a task by ID
- POST /tasks - Create a new task
- Request body validation
- Custom AppError class
- Centralized error handling
- Not-found middleware
- Consistent JSON error responses
- Safe 500 error responses without stack traces
- Tasks stored in tasks.json

## Installation

Install dependencies:

npm install

## Run the Server

Start the server:

npm start

Default URL:

http://localhost:3000

To use a different port in PowerShell:

$env:PORT=4000
npm start

## Task Format

A task must contain:

{
  "id": 999,
  "title": "Learn Express",
  "completed": false,
  "priority": "high"
}

Allowed priority values:

- low
- medium
- high

## API Endpoints

### Health Check

GET /health

Example:

curl.exe http://localhost:3000/health

Expected status:

200 OK

### Get All Tasks

GET /tasks

Example:

curl.exe http://localhost:3000/tasks

Expected status:

200 OK

### Get Task by ID

GET /tasks/:id

Example:

curl.exe http://localhost:3000/tasks/201

Expected status:

200 OK

### Create a Task

POST /tasks

PowerShell example:

$body = @{
    id = 999
    title = "Learn Express"
    completed = $false
    priority = "high"
} | ConvertTo-Json

Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://localhost:3000/tasks" -Method POST -ContentType "application/json" -Body $body

Expected status:

201 Created

## Validation

The API validates:

- id must be an integer
- title must be a non-empty string
- completed must be true or false
- priority must be low, medium, or high

Invalid data returns:

400 Bad Request

## Error Handling

The API uses a consistent JSON error format:

{
  "error": {
    "code": "ERROR_CODE",
    "message": "Human-readable message",
    "details": null
  }
}

Common errors:

- INVALID_JSON - 400
- VALIDATION_ERROR - 400
- DUPLICATE_TASK_ID - 400
- TASK_NOT_FOUND - 404
- ROUTE_NOT_FOUND - 404
- INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR - 500

## Error Testing

The API should handle:

- Invalid payload -> 400
- Malformed JSON -> 400
- Unknown task ID -> 404
- Unknown route -> 404
- Duplicate task ID -> 400
- Unexpected server error -> 500

Unexpected errors return a safe message:

{
  "error": {
    "code": "INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR",
    "message": "Internal server error",
    "details": null
  }
}

Stack traces are not returned to clients.

